From 4399bcd680e7bf7938c3040cb1c3fbd220d9a071 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Red Daka <emmanuel.rayan.daka@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 20 Aug 2026 07:18:29 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Fix database type-safety: remove as-never/as-any casts on
 Supabase queries
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The generated Database type in src/integrations/supabase/types.ts has been
correctly in sync with the migrations for a while, but 35+ call sites across
12 files still bypassed it with `.from("table" as never)`, `(supabase as any)`,
or `payload as any` on inserts/updates. These were leftover workarounds from
before types.ts included tables like dear_today, comments, profiles,
bookmarks, collections, volumes, and seasons — once the types caught up, the
casts should have been removed but weren't, so the compiler stopped checking
table names, column names, and insert/update shapes on nearly all
comment/bookmark/profile/taxonomy/dear-today queries.

Removing the casts surfaced one real bug: in account/bookmarks.tsx, the
per-content-type table lookup was typed as a plain `string` instead of a
real Supabase table-name literal, and the joined "meta" row was typed `any`.
Both are now properly typed against the Database schema
(TableName = keyof Database["public"]["Tables"]).

Verified: `tsc --noEmit` and `vite build` both pass clean with zero
`as never` / `as any` casts remaining in application code (routeTree.gen.ts,
which is auto-generated by the TanStack Router codegen, is unaffected and
untouched).
